======================================================
The Structure of the Test Cases Directory
======================================================


The directory 'tests' contains the files used to test the modeled TEE APIs.
Below are brief descriptions of each file & subdirectory.

- main.maude    	            : Functions used to run test cases (test runner).

- Unit test cases (files in 'cases')

  - test-generic.maude.      	: Test cases for Generic Object API.
  - test-transient.maude     	: Test cases for Transient Object API. 
  - test-persistent.maude    	: Test cases for Persistent Object API.
  - test-data-stream.maude   	: Test cases for Data Stream Access API.
  - test-enumerator.maude    	: Test cases for Persistent Object Enumeration API.
  - test-cryptographic.maude 	: Test cases for Cryptographic Operations API.
  - aux.maude                 : Function used to define test cases.

- API-level black-box regression tests (files in 'api')

  - The 96 searches check external API calls and return values, using the
    abstract top-level handle model and current GlobalPlatform API states.
  - Run all of them with: python3 tests/run-api-suite.py
  - The runner uses MAUDE_BIN when set, then checks sibling
    tee-formal-analysis and zenodo/tee-formal-analysis checkouts,
    and finally searches PATH for maude.

- completion/<group>.maude   : Regression searches for completed GP API paths,
                               split by API group (crypto, transient, ...).
- gp-conformance/<group>.maude : Focused reductions derived from GP v1.3.1,
                               split by the module each red uses (core, crypto, ...).
